{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/rang/register-regenerated.sh","title":"The register-regeneration measure can never fail when make gen changes other files, though its header says it stops at the first problem","severity":"low","source":"conventions","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"If regenerating changes some other file, the acceptance check only warns and still reports success. Today nothing is broken, but a dirty tree could slip through unnoticed.","can_cu":"Low impact: nothing is wrong today, and the check can be tightened later at small cost without affecting users.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/card.html","title":"The human-facing card still shows the old Vietnamese folder path, which no longer exists after the English rename","severity":"low","source":"conventions","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The card shown to the approver names a folder under its old name, which no longer exists. A reader may be briefly confused, but the rename is recorded elsewhere.","can_cu":"Cosmetic only, no data or behaviour affected, and the decision log is append-only so correcting it costs more than it gains.","proposal":"wont-fix","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"tools/design-assembly/check.mjs","title":"Lint re-run says a decision is held by the named rule even when that rule never fires; spacing stays green with no-off-scale-spacing turned off","severity":"high","source":"bugs","inContract":true,"acRef":"AC-2","plain":"","can_cu":"","proposal":"","khongBacBo":false,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"tools/design-assembly/components.mjs","title":"Register lists every re-exported component a second time, with no props, under the barrel file","severity":"medium","source":"bugs","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"Nine filter components appear twice in the component register, once with full details and once empty. An agent looking one up can get two conflicting answers about the same component.","can_cu":"Moderate: it can mislead whoever reads the register, but nothing is lost, and a separate fix to the register tool is cleaner than patching it inside this adoption.","proposal":"new-contract","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/rang/register-regenerated.sh","title":"register-regenerated.sh runs make gen on the real repository, so the evidence is overwritten and a second run passes","severity":"medium","source":"bugs","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"If the register is out of date, the acceptance check rewrites it while checking, so a second run looks fine. The first run does report the problem, and today the register is current.","can_cu":"Low risk now because the first run still fails visibly; it only matters when the register goes stale, and the working tree shows the change.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/rang/lint-rule-off.mjs","title":"exit() inside try skips finally, leaving the temporary linked copies behind","severity":"low","source":"bugs","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"When an acceptance check fails, two temporary folders are left behind on the machine. The check result itself is correct.","can_cu":"Harmless clutter in a temp directory that the system cleans up, so the fix is not worth opening work.","proposal":"wont-fix","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"tests/design-registry.test.ts","title":"Hình dạng 5 — tuyên quét LỚP nhưng chỉ có điểm-case: «mỗi linh kiện xuất ra là một mục có file, level, source»","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The test claims every component has a file, level and source but only spot-checks a few. A component missing one of these could go unnoticed.","can_cu":"The register is generated by a tool and currently correct, so the risk is small and the test can be strengthened later cheaply.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"tests/design-registry.test.ts","title":"Hình dạng 5 — tuyên quét LỚP nhưng chỉ có điểm-case: «both bought libraries as libraries, and the templates folder as templates»","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The test says all bought-library components are labelled as libraries but checks only one per folder. A wrongly labelled component elsewhere would not be caught.","can_cu":"Mislabelling would be a cosmetic register error, easy to spot and fix, and none exists now.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"tests/design-registry.test.ts","title":"Hình dạng 4 — assertion âm tính đứng một mình: SidebarSeparator không có variants","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"One test would still pass even if the separator component vanished from the register. The register is correct today.","can_cu":"Tiny risk: another test already covers the register's presence of components broadly, and it is a one-line strengthening later.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/rang/register-regenerated.sh","title":"Hình dạng 3 (kèm 1) — grep chuỗi lệnh trong mk/design.mk thay vì kiểm quan hệ mục đích → lệnh, và thay vì quan sát make gen hay make check","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The acceptance check looks for the right commands in the build file but not under the right step, so a misplaced command might still pass. The build file is correct now.","can_cu":"Only matters if someone later moves those commands, and the normal check run would likely expose it.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/rang/owner-answers.mjs","title":"Hình dạng 3 — đếm và ngưỡng thay cho quan hệ cặp màu sáng/tối của phép kiểm tương phản","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The check counts four contrast tests but does not confirm they cover light and dark modes for both colour pairs. A wrong set of four would still pass.","can_cu":"The actual data is correct today, and a bad contrast setting would be visible and reversible.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/rang/lint-rule-off.mjs","title":"Hình dạng 5 — thẻ hứa «tắt một luật lint đang giữ quyết định» (lớp chín luật) nhưng chỉ lật một luật; tám luật còn lại chỉ dựa vào nhãn tự khai của công cụ","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The card tells the owner that turning off any of nine rules will raise an alarm, but only one rule was actually tested that way. The other eight rely on the tool's own labels.","can_cu":"The overclaim is on the card wording, and a real gap in one of the eight would be caught by the other finding about the lint re-run.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-14T14:23:20Z","sha":"c374679a21edc3ef5d170fe64a2f423b4095e4a6","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/adopt-design-assembly/rang/lint-rerun.mjs","title":"Hình dạng 5 — «đúng chín phép kiểm loại lint» không được đếm; số 9 in ra là hằng","severity":"low","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The check prints that there are nine lint checks without actually counting them, so an extra duplicate would not be noticed. The count is right today.","can_cu":"Low impact: only a future accidental duplicate would slip through, and it is easy to correct later.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
